.TH ANAME-MATERIALIZE 1 "2026-08-18" "rgbdns 0.6.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aname-materialize \- replace rgbdns ANAME directives with address records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aname-materialize
.RI [ data
.RI [ data.materialized
.RI [ dnssec ]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolves each private rgbdns ANAME directive into ordinary owner A and AAAA
records, respecting its TTL ceiling, then atomically writes tinydns text. If
no ANAME exists, the input records pass through unchanged. Resolution failure
does not replace the destination.
.PP
With a DNSSEC policy argument, only ANAME directives in K zones are
materialized; directives in explicit U zones pass through unchanged.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, 100 for usage errors, and 111 for operational failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rgbsec-sign (1),
.BR tinydns-data (1),
.BR rgbdns (7)
